  "reason": "RNA multiprofile scvi avgpool is strong (0.650 acc, 0.628 F1), and multimodal scvi/resnet avgpool weighted is the current best (0.678 acc, 0.646 F1), but only modestly above RNA-only, while image-only single resnet is very weak (0.208 acc). The key uncertainty is whether the image modality can contribute at all under the multiprofile/avgpool setting used in the best multimodal runs. config_011 tests image-only with the same resnet encoder, multiprofile setting, and avgpool aggregation, isolating the image stream’s contribution before investing further in multimodal or stronger image encoders. This is a high-value, budget-efficient experiment because it clarifies whether future effort should focus on image representation/fusion or primarily on RNA-side design choices."
}

